myelin 1
id      angular
about   Angular 22 (@angular/core 22.2): bans APIs deprecated or removed in 18 to 22 (*ngIf, HttpClientModule, withFetch, provideRoutes, ComponentFactoryResolver, platform-browser-dynamic, @angular/animations, Hammer, moduleId) that models still write
fires   angular | @angular | ngmodule | bootstrapApplication | provideRouter | HttpClient | ngIf | ngFor | @Component
comments skip
status  Researched 2026-10-26 against @angular/core 22.2.3 (npm latest). Sourced from the angular/angular CHANGELOG and the adev docs source on GitHub (angular.dev was unreachable from the research sandbox). Regex-level checks; bench corpus passes; snippets not compiled or run.

= version     @angular/core 22.2.3, @angular/cli 22.2.4 (npm latest, 2026-10-14 / 2026-10-22)
= verified    2026-10-26
= typescript  TypeScript 6 is required from 22.0; older versions are no longer supported
= templates   @if / @for (track) / @switch are the control flow; *ngIf / *ngFor / *ngSwitch are deprecated since 20.0
= components  standalone by default since 19.0; OnPush by default since 22.0 (ChangeDetectionStrategy.Eager keeps the old behaviour)
= reactivity  input() / input.required() / output() / model() / viewChild() are the signal APIs; the decorators remain supported
= bootstrap   bootstrapApplication(App, appConfig) with provideRouter(routes) and provideHttpClient(...) in appConfig
= zone        zoneless by default since 21.0; zone.js and provideZoneChangeDetection are opt-in
= http        fetch is the default backend since 22.0; HttpClientModule deprecated since 18.0; JSONP deprecated since 22.1

! A1 /\*ng(?:If|For(?:Of)?|Switch(?:Case|Default)?)\b/   *ngIf / *ngFor / *ngSwitch are deprecated since Angular 20. Use @if / @for (with track) / @switch blocks. -> $control
! A2 /\bHttpClient(?:Module|XsrfModule)\b/   HttpClientModule and HttpClientXsrfModule are deprecated. Use provideHttpClient(...) in appConfig providers, with functional interceptors registered through withInterceptors(...). -> $http
! A3 /\bwithFetch\s*\(/   withFetch() is deprecated in 22.0 and redundant: fetch is the default HttpClient backend. Remove it. -> $config
! A4 /\breportProgress\s*:/   The reportProgress option is deprecated in 22.0. Use reportUploadProgress and reportDownloadProgress instead. -> $service
! A5 /\bwithJsonpSupport\s*\(|\bHttpClientJsonpModule\b|\b[hH]ttp\w*\.jsonp\s*(?:<[^>]*>)?\(/   JSONP support is deprecated since 22.1 (HttpClient.jsonp, withJsonpSupport, HttpClientJsonpModule). Use a standard request, or CORS.
! A6 /\bprovideRoutes\s*\(/   provideRoutes() was removed in 22.0. Register routes with provideRouter(routes) or the ROUTES multi token, and guard them with functions in canActivate. -> $guard
! A7 /\bComponentFactoryResolver\b|\bComponentFactory\b/   ComponentFactoryResolver and ComponentFactory were removed in 22.0. Pass the component class to ViewContainerRef.createComponent(Cmp) directly.
! A8 /\bcreateNgModuleRef\b/   createNgModuleRef was removed in 22.0. Use createNgModule instead.
! A9 /\.checkNoChanges\s*\(/   ChangeDetectorRef.checkNoChanges was removed in 22.0. In tests call fixture.detectChanges() instead.
! A10 /\bHammerModule\b|\bHAMMER_GESTURE_CONFIG\b|\bHammerGestureConfig\b|['"]hammerjs['"]/   Hammer.js integration was deprecated in 20.0 and removed in 22.0. Use pointer events or your own gesture code.
! A11 /@angular\/platform-browser-dynamic\b|\bplatformBrowserDynamic\s*\(/   @angular/platform-browser-dynamic is deprecated since 20.0. Bootstrap with bootstrapApplication from @angular/platform-browser. -> $main
! A12 /from\s+['"]@angular\/animations(?:\/[\w\/-]+)?['"]/   The @angular/animations package is deprecated since 20.2. Use CSS transitions and animations, or the animate.enter / animate.leave bindings.
! A13 /\banimations\s*:\s*\[\s*trigger\s*\(/   The animations field on @Component is deprecated since 20.2 (it depends on @angular/animations). Use CSS transitions instead.
! A14 /\bprovideExperimentalZonelessChangeDetection\b/   provideExperimentalZonelessChangeDetection was renamed in 20.0. Zoneless is the default from 21.0, so the provider is not needed. -> $config
! A15 /\bmoduleId\s*:\s*module\.id\b/   moduleId was removed from @Component metadata in 21.0. Delete the line; Angular resolves templates relative to the component. -> $signals
! A16 /\binterpolation\s*:\s*\[/   The interpolation option on @Component was removed in 21.0 (it was deprecated in 18.0). Only the default {{ }} delimiters are supported. -> $signals

~ P1 Bootstrap new apps with bootstrapApplication(App, appConfig). The docs say the team recommends it over bootstrapModule for all new code. -> $main
~ P2 Put routing, HTTP and interceptors in an ApplicationConfig providers array: provideRouter(routes), provideHttpClient(withInterceptors([...])). Avoid RouterModule.forRoot and NgModule imports in new code. -> $config
~ P3 Use the signal APIs in new code: input() / input.required(), output(), model(), viewChild() / viewChildren(). The @Input, @Output and @ViewChild decorators are still supported, so do not rewrite working code only for this. -> $signals
~ P4 For a new singleton service, use @Service() with inject(). Keep @Injectable() when you need constructor DI, useClass / useValue / useExisting, or a non-root scope. -> $service
~ P5 Write route guards and resolvers as functions (CanActivateFn, ResolveFn) that call inject(). Redirect by returning a UrlTree, not false followed by navigate. -> $guard
~ P6 Use functional interceptors (withInterceptors) rather than class-based HTTP_INTERCEPTORS with withInterceptorsFromDi(). The docs recommend them for predictable ordering. -> $http
~ P7 Use @if / @for / @switch in new templates. Only use @for with a track expression. -> $control
~ P8 Components are standalone by default since 19.0. Omit standalone: true; use standalone: false only for a component that is still declared in an NgModule.
~ P9 Components are OnPush by default in 22.0. Omit changeDetection unless you need ChangeDetectionStrategy.Eager to keep the old behaviour.
~ P10 Apps on Angular 21 and later run zoneless by default. Do not add zone.js to polyfills or provideZoneChangeDetection() to a new app. -> $config

$ main
import { bootstrapApplication } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { App } from './app/app';
import { appConfig } from './app/app.config';

bootstrapApplication(App, appConfig).catch((err) => console.error(err));
$$

$ config
import { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core';
import { provideHttpClient, withInterceptors } from '@angular/common/http';
import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';
import { routes } from './app.routes';
import { authInterceptor } from './auth.interceptor';

export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {
  providers: [
    provideRouter(routes),
    provideHttpClient(withInterceptors([authInterceptor])),
  ],
};
$$

$ http
import { HttpInterceptorFn } from '@angular/common/http';

export const authInterceptor: HttpInterceptorFn = (req, next) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
  return next(token ? req.clone({ setHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } }) : req);
};
$$

$ guard
import { inject } from '@angular/core';
import { CanActivateFn, Router } from '@angular/router';
import { AuthService } from './auth.service';

export const authGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {
  const auth = inject(AuthService);
  const router = inject(Router);
  return auth.isLoggedIn() ? true : router.parseUrl('/login');
};
$$

$ control
@if (user(); as u) {
  <p>Signed in as {{ u.name }}</p>
} @else {
  <p>Please sign in.</p>
}

@for (todo of todos(); track todo.id) {
  <li [class.done]="todo.done">{{ todo.title }}</li>
} @empty {
  <li>Nothing to do.</li>
}

@switch (status()) {
  @case ('loading') { <p>Loading...</p> }
  @case ('error') { <p>Could not load the list.</p> }
  @default { <p>Ready.</p> }
}
$$

$ signals
import { Component, ElementRef, input, model, output, viewChild } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-counter',
  template: `
    <p>{{ label() }}</p>
    <button #btn (click)="onClick()">{{ value() }}</button>
  `,
})
export class Counter {
  label = input.required<string>();
  increment = input(1);
  value = model(0);
  reset = output<void>();
  button = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLButtonElement>>('btn');

  onClick() {
    this.value.update((v) => v + this.increment());
  }

  clear() {
    this.value.set(0);
    this.reset.emit();
  }
}
$$

$ service
import { inject, Service } from '@angular/core';
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';

export interface Todo {
  id: number;
  title: string;
  done: boolean;
}

@Service()
export class TodoStore {
  private readonly http = inject(HttpClient);

  load() {
    return this.http.get<Todo[]>('/api/todos');
  }

  upload(file: File) {
    const body = new FormData();
    body.append('file', file);
    return this.http.post('/api/todos/import', body, { reportUploadProgress: true, observe: 'events' });
  }
}
$$
